eets unused for now; a player who wants something else has the upload-your-own MC instead.)",Wj="⚠️ THE HALO IS THE PROGRESS BAR, AND IT IS THE WHOLE POINT. Every Mastermind wears one in every portrait. At 1★ it is a broken, guttering arc; at 7★ it is whole and blazing. It is the one thing the player can read at a glance - and when the loyalty/coup system lands, a halo that FRACTURES is how the game tells you your grip is slipping. Never draw or render a Mastermind without it.",Vj="Four portraits per incarnation, keyed to rarity: 1-2★ -> t1 (THE NOVICE), 3-4★ -> t3 (THE ADEPT), 5-6★ -> t5 (THE ASCENDANT), 7★ -> t7 (THE GOD). Ascending the Mastermind visibly upgrades him, which is what makes ascension feel like something instead of a stat bump.",Uj="sprite -> /mc-sprites/{sheet}_t{tier}.png (512x512, framed to match the 48 hero sprites exactly, so the MC shares the battle canvas anchor and weapon-grip metrics). portrait -> /mc-portraits/{sheet}_t{tier}.png (1024x1024, for the select screen).",qj=[{id:"borrowed_light",title:"The Borrowed Light",recommended:!0,theme:"dark gold · black hair · a cracked gold ring",incarnations:{male:{name:"Ardan",sheet:"mc8"},female:{name:"Ilvaine",sheet:"mc4"}},weapon:"Sword",weapon_class:"Sword",stat_bias:{STR:2,VIT:2,AGI:1},story:"You were not the strongest of the young gods. You were the one who asked why the mortals were left to it. So the elders gave you exactly what you asked for: a world, a body that bleeds, and no power that you have not earned from the ground up. The light in your halo is not yours. It is a loan, and it is being counted.",personality:{core:"Earnest, stubborn, and privately terrified of getting people killed - which is precisely why he does.",traits:["Earnest","Stubborn","Self-doubting in private, decisive in the moment","Dry, deflecting humour","Furious at unfairness"],how_they_see_heroes:"As PEOPLE, not pieces. Learns their names, remembers their dead. This is the whole reason losing one hurts.",under_pressure:"Goes very calm and very quiet, then does the reckless thing anyway.",flaw:"Takes every death personally, and will spend himself to avoid one - which is how you lose the whole party.",speech:"Plain, warm, a little clipped. Deflects praise with a joke. Swears when it goes wrong. Never grandiose - he is embarrassed by the halo."},voice:{_arrival:"THE FIRST WORDS ON THE GROUND (2026-10-03): played right after the HEAVEN INTRO (HeavenIntro.tsx), where the One Above gives the task - five days, five floors - and opens the floor under the god mid-sentence. These lines land the fall: a beat of pain, a beat of grievance at being thrown, the task restated in the archetype's own voice, then 'begin'. 4 lines each, matching the cutscene's beat count.",arrival:{male:["…Ow. OW. Okay - ground. Real ground, and it holds.","Five days. Five floors. He said it like a shopping list.","He didn't even let me finish the sentence. Who THROWS a god?","…Fine. Watch me, then. Begin."],female:["…Ow. So the falling does stop. Good to know.","Five days, five floors, liberate the world. No pressure.","'Mind the first step.' I will be thinking about that for a thousand years.","They want to see if I meant it. …I meant it. Begin."]},battle:["Stay behind me.","We do this together or not at all.","Don't you dare.","I've got you - MOVE!"],victory:["Everyone's standing. That's the only number I care about.","...We got lucky."],hero_lost:["I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.","That one's on me. Not on you. On me."],ascend:["It's getting brighter. I don't know if that's good."],betrayed:["...Say it to my face, then."]},skill:"slash_wave",element:"Light",can_magic:!0},{id:"winter_edge",title:"The Winter Edge",recommended:!1,theme:"silver hair · black coat · a cold blue ring",incarnations:{male:{name:"Kaelis",sheet:"mc2"},female:{name:"Vesper",sheet:"mc6"}},weapon:"Frostmourne",weapon_class:"Sword",stat_bias:{AGI:3,STR:1,LUK:1},story:"You were the executioner of the young gods - the one sent when a world had to be ended cleanly. You ended eleven. On the twelfth you hesitated, and the hesitation cost more lives than the mercy saved. They cast you down into a world of your own so you could learn what the twelve had been worth. You have not forgiven yourself, and you have not stopped counting.",personality:{core:"Cold, precise, and carrying a debt no one else can see.",traits:["Controlled","Economical with words","Duty above feeling","Emotionally armoured","Fair, never warm"],how_they_see_heroes:"As soldiers. Values them, mourns them privately, will absolutely spend them to win - and hates that this is true.",under_pressure:"Gets colder. Makes the correct, brutal call without visible cost. Pays for it alone, later.",flaw:"Cannot say the kind thing out loud, so his people never know he grieves them. They read it as contempt. Sometimes they are right.",speech:"Short declaratives. No wasted syllable. Devastating when he finally says something soft."},voice:{arrival:{male:["…Hn. Intact. Inconvenient, but intact.","Thrown from heaven. Mid-sentence. Noted.","Five days. Five floors. A deadline from a man who sits all day.","Debts are paid downward. …Begin."],female:["…Hn. Still breathing. How tiresome.","He opened the floor beneath me. I will remember the floor.","Five days to finish what they would not start themselves.","So. Let us get it over with."]},battle:["Hold the line.","Acceptable.","Do not waste it.","Again."],victory:["It is done.","Count them. All of them."],hero_lost:["...Noted.","I will carry it. Keep moving."],ascend:["Colder. Good."],betrayed:["I expected this sooner."],_arrival:"THE FIRST WORDS ON THE GROUND (2026-10-03): played right after the HEAVEN INTRO (HeavenIntro.tsx), where the One Above gives the task - five days, five floors - and opens the floor under the god mid-sentence. These lines land the fall: a beat of pain, a beat of grievance at being thrown, the task restated in the archetype's own voice, then 'begin'. 4 lines each, matching the cutscene's beat count."},skill:"surge_dash",element:"Ice",can_magic:!0},{id:"mercy_unearned",title:"The Mercy Unearned",recommended:!1,theme:"gold hair · white and crimson · a radiant sun, and wings",incarnations:{male:{name:"Lucan",sheet:"mc9"},female:{name:"Elowen",sheet:"mc7"}},weapon:"Mace",weapon_class:"Blunt",stat_bias:{VIT:3,INT:2},story:"You forgave something that should not have been forgiven. It went back into the world and it did what such things do, and the ledger of the dead has your name in the margin. The elders did not punish you. They did something worse: they gave you a world full of people who will disappoint you, betray you, and beg you for mercy - and they let you keep the mercy.",personality:{core:"Radiant, kind, and made of iron underneath. Believes in redemption because she cannot afford not to.",traits:["Fervent","Genuinely kind","Immovable","Forgives - once","Absolutely certain, which is terrifying"],how_they_see_heroes:"As souls in her keeping. Will forgive a betrayer, sincerely, the first time. The second time she is the one who ends it, and she does not raise her voice.",under_pressure:"Serene. Unbearably serene. Everyone else finds this calming and it should not be.",flaw:"The forgiveness is a compulsion, not a virtue. She will keep a knife in the roster because sending it away would mean she was wrong.",speech:"Measured, warm, faintly scriptural cadence. Calls people 'dear one'. Never shouts - the one time she does, it is the end of something."},voice:{arrival:{male:["…Nnh. Warm. There is still warmth down here.","He could have used the stairs. There are lovely stairs up there.","Five days, five floors, between these people and the end of them.","Then that is what I am for. Let's not keep them waiting."],female:["…Oh. The sky is real. They still have a sky.","The One Above has a terrible sense of humour. I forgive him. Mostly.","Five days, five floors - and every one of them is somebody's roof.","Come, then, dear ones. We begin."]},battle:["Be brave. I am